# Cloudflare Pages redirects — old WordPress URLs -> new single-page site.
# Keeps Google ranking from the old pages instead of 404ing. Specific rules first,
# then a catch-all so ANY old path lands on the homepage rather than a dead end.
# Tidy public URL for the Nomad page (added 2026-08-19). The file stays nomad-site.html on
# purpose: venue_lint.py picks a page's home venue BY FILENAME.
/nomad             /nomad-site  301
/nomad/            /nomad-site  301
/index.html        /            301
# Safety net 2026-08-24: the Nomad page linked back to /levelup-site.html for weeks (404).
# Links are fixed at source to point at `/`; these catch anything Google or a printed card
# still holds. Specific rules only, never a catch-all (see tombstone below).
/levelup-site.html /            301
/levelup-site      /            301
/home              /            301
/blog              /            301
/blog/*            /            301
/events            /#whatson    301
/event             /#whatson    301
/whats-on          /#whatson    301
/booking           /#book       301
/book              /#book       301
/membership        /#pricing    301
/memberships       /#pricing    301
/pricing           /#pricing    301
/prices            /#pricing    301
/games             /#games      301
/game-library      /#games      301
/board-games       /#games      301
/menu              /#nomad      301
/meals             /#nomad      301
/about             /#do         301
/story             /#do         301
/gallery           /#do         301
/friends           /#nomad      301
/contact           /#visit      301
/visit             /#visit      301
# 2026-09-22: the four old WordPress URLs Google STILL lists (site: search) all 404'd.
# Trailing-slash variants are separate paths on Cloudflare Pages, so both are listed.
# There is no #menu anchor on the page; food is the Nomad section, hence /#nomad.
/menu-food-drinks-level-up   /#nomad     301
/menu-food-drinks-level-up/  /#nomad     301
/contact-us                  /#visit     301
/contact-us/                 /#visit     301
/membership-level-up         /#pricing   301
/membership-level-up/        /#pricing   301
/events-level-up             /#whatson   301
/events-level-up/            /#whatson   301

# 🔴 TOMBSTONE 2026-08-19 — DO NOT RE-ADD A CATCH-ALL.
# A greedy `/*  /  301` rule used to live at the bottom of this file. It was removed from the
# DEPLOYED copy on 2026-08-01 (commit 086f9d0, "Fix redirect loop") because it matches `/` itself
# and sends the homepage to the homepage forever, taking the whole site down.
# That fix was never back-ported HERE, so this source file still carried the bad rule. On
# 2026-08-19 this file was copied over the deployed one and took the live site down again for
# about two minutes (`/` and `/nomad-site` both looping) until it was reverted.
# Unmatched paths returning 404 is the CORRECT behaviour. Explicit rules above still work.
